      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm looking at some data for a new roundabout design near a major junction in london. can you give me a quick comparison of how signalized intersections vs roundabouts typically handle traffic throughput and what the main differences are in terms of delay and flow? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Signalized intersections and roundabouts manage traffic flow differently, impacting throughput and delay. Roundabouts generally promote smoother, continuous flow, especially at moderate volumes, as traffic proceeds based on gaps in the circulating stream. In contrast, signalized intersections use fixed timing to manage conflicting movements, which can lead to stop-and-go conditions and higher delays when traffic volumes are high. Overall, roundabouts often reduce delays and emissions by eliminating stops, whereas signals prioritize capacity through controlled stopping.",
